{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-torsion-existence","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-torsion-existence","kind":"remark","title":"$q$-Torsion leaves: existence and Frobenius obstruction","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-torsion-leaf"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","tags":["torsion-leaf","frobenius"],"text":"q-torsion-existence.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-torsion-existence\"></a><p>Maximal integral submanifolds of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> are Legendrian submanifolds. A <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-torsion leaf is a Legendrian submanifold invariant under the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Reeb flow. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code>, the deformation generically breaks periodicity, demanding KAM-type persistence results. The failure of the Frobenius structure on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> forces the dimension bound and gives <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-torsion leaves their rigidity.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-torsion-existence.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.20.8","page":"b/rem-q-torsion-existence","qa":{"counts":{"pass":58,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":50},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
